From dc4f3684c053dabdd50da3940e010ae18f8d1b02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dsh-agent <agent@local>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:57:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(session): contain non-JSON projection values at every
 carrier

A projection unit whose state or wire view leaves the JSON value set failed the
whole checkpoint record (the cache stays stale at the previous cut because the
write is fail-soft) and the whole forwarded host event (the client never
receives the session), so one field of one plugin removed session availability:
fork rolled back and the listing row vanished on reconnect.

The same input reached three more carriers, where it corrupts instead of
throwing: a Remote stream item's only serialization is JSON.stringify with no
JSON check, so a control baseline cell, a control change frame, and the
session/follow projections block would each publish a structurally valid value
that is semantically wrong (a Map as {}) with no warning anywhere. Every one of
these carriers had assumed a value accepted by a unit's viewSchema is JSON-safe;
viewSchema is Zod validation, which accepts a Map, a Date, or an object holding
undefined.

Each carrier now degrades at its own granularity and none reinterprets a
business value: the cache omits the offending row (an absent row is already that
key's refold floor) and losslessProjectionValues() drops the offending cell for
the listing hints, the control baseline, and the follow block, each warning with
the key and session id; the control change feed drops a frame the Client could
only receive corrupted. asOfSeq stays the registry's cut everywhere, so an
omission can only overstate staleness, and isJsonValue keeps its strictness.

